00:12:06.320 --> 00:12:12.399
personalized books need an ISBN?" The

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:15.360
answer is no. Most personalized

00:12:12.399 --> 00:12:18.000
children's books do not need an ISBN.

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:20.320
And here is why. An ISBN, which stands

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:22.800
for International Standard Book number,

00:12:20.320 --> 00:12:25.040
is used for traditionally published

00:12:22.800 --> 00:12:28.160
books. These are books that are intended

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:30.639
for wide retail distribution. For

00:12:28.160 --> 00:12:32.320
example, books sold in bookstores, books

00:12:30.639 --> 00:12:34.800
sold through places like Books a

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:37.040
Million, Barnes & Noble, general books

00:12:34.800 --> 00:12:39.120
on Amazon. Personalized books are

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:42.720
different. Okay? You're not offering a

00:12:39.120 --> 00:12:45.360
product with a fixed text, a fixed

00:12:42.720 --> 00:12:48.399
story, and fixed photos. You are

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:50.639
actually creating a custom keepsake

00:12:48.399 --> 00:12:52.880
product. Names change throughout the

00:12:50.639 --> 00:12:54.720
book. Sometimes the photos change

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:57.120
throughout the book, the customized

00:12:54.720 --> 00:12:59.200
characters, the title is always going to

00:12:57.120 --> 00:13:02.000
be changing. And this actually puts the

00:12:59.200 --> 00:13:05.279
customized books in the same category as

00:13:02.000 --> 00:13:08.480
keepsake gifts, personalized journals,

00:13:05.279 --> 00:13:09.920
custom photo books, memory books, etc.

00:13:08.480 --> 00:13:13.040
These are actually then treated as

00:13:09.920 --> 00:13:14.959
custom merchandise and not fixed books.

